@page "/business-value"

<PageTitle>Business Value - OperationsFlow</PageTitle>

<div class="operations-dashboard business-value-page">
    <PageIntro Eyebrow="Business Case"
               Title="Business Value"
               Subtitle="A practical explanation of the value OperationsFlow creates for safety/compliance review, admin workflow, reporting, accountability, and management follow-up.">
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="implementation-plan">Implementation Plan</a>
        <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="prototype-scope">Prototype Scope</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="reports">Reports</a>
    </PageIntro>

    <div class="page-purpose-note">
        <strong>Purpose:</strong> use this page to explain why OperationsFlow matters to a business. The value is not only the screens — it is the reduced missed follow-up, clearer ownership, cleaner reporting, and better visibility across safety, compliance, admin, and operations.
    </div>

    <section class="kpi-grid">
        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Main Value</span>
            <strong>Follow-up</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Less work falling through gaps</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Business Area</span>
            <strong>OSHE</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Safety / compliance / admin</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Visibility</span>
            <strong>Owner-based</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Who owns what next</span>
        </div>

        <div class="kpi-card">
            <span class="kpi-label">Reporting</span>
            <strong>Ready</strong>
            <span class="kpi-note">Meeting and management review</span>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid business-value-hero-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel business-value-main-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>The Core Business Problem</h2>
                    <p>OperationsFlow is designed around a common problem in small and medium businesses.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <p class="business-value-copy">
                Important follow-up work often starts in emails, conversations, inspections, safety meetings,
                paper forms, spreadsheets, or document folders. Without a connected workflow, it becomes hard
                to see what is overdue, who owns the next step, what has already been reviewed, and what needs
                to be escalated before it becomes a bigger issue.
            </p>

            <div class="business-problem-grid">
                <article>
                    <span>01</span>
                    <strong>Missed follow-up</strong>
                    <p>Corrective actions, document reviews, training expiries, and admin tasks can sit unnoticed.</p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <span>02</span>
                    <strong>Weak ownership</strong>
                    <p>People may know something needs doing, but the system does not make ownership clear.</p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <span>03</span>
                    <strong>Manual reporting</strong>
                    <p>Managers often need to rebuild status summaries from scattered records before meetings.</p>
                </article>

                <article>
                    <span>04</span>
                    <strong>Poor traceability</strong>
                    <p>When records change, it can be hard to see what changed, when, and why.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>OperationsFlow Response</h2>
                    <p>How the prototype answers that problem.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="business-value-highlight">
                <span>Value proposition</span>
                <strong>One place to review what needs attention next</strong>
                <p>
                    OperationsFlow brings operational work, corrective actions, risk review, training,
                    document control, document intake, reminders, workload, reports, activity history,
                    and data quality into one connected workflow view.
                </p>
            </div>

            <ul class="action-list">
                <li>Shows overdue and due-soon work before it is forgotten.</li>
                <li>Groups work by owner so follow-up responsibility is visible.</li>
                <li>Turns safety/compliance review into a meeting-ready workflow.</li>
                <li>Creates reporting views that support weekly and monthly management review.</li>
                <li>Uses activity history and data quality checks to improve accountability.</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="business-value-card-grid">
        @foreach (var value in ValueCards)
        {
            <article class="business-value-card">
                <div class="business-value-card-header">
                    <span>@value.Number</span>
                    <div>
                        <p class="eyebrow">@value.Category</p>
                        <h2>@value.Title</h2>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <p>@value.Description</p>

                <ul>
                    @foreach (var item in value.Items)
                    {
                        <li>@item</li>
                    }
                </ul>
            </article>
        }
    </section>

    <section class="report-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Business Value Matrix</h2>
                <p>How each part of OperationsFlow contributes to practical business outcomes.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <table class="report-table business-value-table">
            <thead>
                <tr>
                    <th>Business Need</th>
                    <th>OperationsFlow Feature</th>
                    <th>Value Created</th>
                    <th>Example Review Question</th>
                </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
                @foreach (var item in ValueMatrix)
                {
                    <tr>
                        <td><strong>@item.BusinessNeed</strong></td>
                        <td><span class="@item.BadgeClass">@item.Feature</span></td>
                        <td>@item.ValueCreated</td>
                        <td>@item.ReviewQuestion</td>
                    </tr>
                }
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </section>

    <section class="summary-grid">
        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Before vs After</h2>
                    <p>The practical shift this project demonstrates.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="before-after-grid">
                <article class="before-card">
                    <span>Before</span>
                    <h3>Scattered follow-up</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Actions spread across emails, meetings, notes, and spreadsheets.</li>
                        <li>Manual chasing required to confirm progress.</li>
                        <li>Reports rebuilt only when someone asks for them.</li>
                        <li>Hard to identify who is overloaded or what is overdue.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>

                <article class="after-card">
                    <span>After</span>
                    <h3>Connected workflow</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Work is tracked with owner, due date, status, priority, and notes.</li>
                        <li>Overdue and due-soon items appear in review views automatically.</li>
                        <li>Reports, workload, reminders, and data quality reuse the same records.</li>
                        <li>Managers can review follow-up without rebuilding the story from scratch.</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="summary-panel">
            <div class="panel-header">
                <div>
                    <h2>Where Value Shows Up</h2>
                    <p>The pages that make the business case visible.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="business-link-list">
                @foreach (var link in BusinessLinks)
                {
                    <a href="@link.Url">
                        <span>@link.Label</span>
                        <strong>@link.Title</strong>
                        <p>@link.Description</p>
                    </a>
                }
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="report-card business-summary-card">
        <div class="panel-header">
            <div>
                <h2>Business Case Summary</h2>
                <p>A short summary that can be used in a portfolio review, demo, or message.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="business-case-summary">
            <p>
                OperationsFlow demonstrates how a business can move from scattered manual follow-up to a
                connected workflow system. It creates value by making overdue work visible, assigning clear
                owners, supporting safety/compliance meetings, improving document and training review,
                exposing data quality issues, and giving managers reporting views without needing to rebuild
                everything manually from spreadsheets or emails.
            </p>

            <p>
                The strongest business value is in safety/compliance and admin follow-up: the same records
                support the Safety Meeting Pack, Compliance Calendar, Workload, Reminders, Reports, Activity Log,
                and Data Quality pages. That makes OperationsFlow a practical example of business systems thinking,
                workflow design, reporting, and production-aware planning.
            </p>
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

